# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# opt-dpu: the host has a DPU/SmartNIC, so the host is not the dataplane.
#
# This is the case that inverts the usual argument.  With a Nitro-class DPU,
# the overlay is terminated on the card: the card does encap/decap, security
# groups, connection tracking and rate limiting, and presents the guest a
# virtio-net or SR-IOV VF directly.  The host kernel never touches a tenant
# packet.
#
# So everything the software dataplane needs becomes attack surface for a job
# nobody is doing on this machine: OVS, the bridge, VXLAN/GENEVE encap, tc
# actions, conntrack.  That is roughly 1MB of code and, more to the point, a
# large amount of packet-parsing logic reachable from tenant traffic.
#
# What a DPU host does still need: device assignment (VFIO/iommufd), SR-IOV,
# PCIe hotplug, and the vendor's VFIO variant driver for VF live migration.
# Those stay in layer-hypervisor.config.
#
#     make PROFILE=hypervisor-dpu build
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG_OPENVSWITCH is not set
# CONFIG_OPENVSWITCH_VXLAN is not set
# CONFIG_OPENVSWITCH_GENEVE is not set
# CONFIG_BRIDGE is not set
# CONFIG_BRIDGE_VLAN_FILTERING is not set
# CONFIG_VXLAN is not set
# CONFIG_GENEVE is not set
# CONFIG_MACVLAN is not set
# CONFIG_MACVTAP is not set
# CONFIG_IPVLAN is not set
# CONFIG_NET_CLS_ACT is not set
# CONFIG_NET_CLS_BPF is not set
# CONFIG_NET_ACT_BPF is not set
# CONFIG_NET_ACT_MIRRED is not set
# CONFIG_NET_ACT_CT is not set
# The tc-flower offload set from layer-hypervisor follows the rest of the
# actions out.  Not optional bookkeeping: NET_ACT_GACT / NET_ACT_TUNNEL_KEY /
# NET_ACT_POLICE each `select NET_CLS_ACT`, so leaving any of them =y would
# resurrect the line above and fail check-config.  The two classifiers go for
# the same reason the ingress qdisc does below -- there is nothing left to
# classify for.
# CONFIG_NET_CLS_FLOWER is not set
# CONFIG_NET_CLS_MATCHALL is not set
# CONFIG_NET_ACT_GACT is not set
# CONFIG_NET_ACT_TUNNEL_KEY is not set
# CONFIG_NET_ACT_POLICE is not set
# CONFIG_NET_TC_SKB_EXT is not set
# CONFIG_NF_FLOW_TABLE is not set
# CONFIG_NF_CONNTRACK_EVENTS is not set
# The ingress qdisc exists to run tc filters, which is the thing being removed.
# CONFIG_NET_SCH_INGRESS is not set
# Per-instance rate limiting is on the card here -- that is in this fragment's
# first paragraph -- so the shaping qdiscs layer-hypervisor adds for the
# software dataplane have no tap to sit on.  ETS is NOT stripped: it schedules
# classes on the host's OWN uplink (management, NVMe-oF), which still exists,
# the same reason fq / fq_codel / mqprio stay.
# CONFIG_NET_SCH_HTB is not set
# CONFIG_NET_SCH_TBF is not set
# CONFIG_MLX5_TC_CT is not set
# CONFIG_MLX5_CLS_ACT is not set

# The host still needs a management interface and its own connectivity, so
# the base IP stack, nftables and NVMe-oF stay.
